/-!
# Bernstein certificate for the near-uniform dual bound (NU)

Paper E, `lem:fqe-near-uniform-dual`: the polynomial inequality `G(x, v) ≥ 0` on
`0 ≤ x ≤ 1/25`, `|v| ≤ 3/25` behind the rational comparisons of NU-2/NU-3, where
`G = (V + xW) - x(V+xW)²/2 + x²(V+xW)³/3 - x³(V+xW)⁴/4 - r L⁺ ((c+d) - b v - γ x)`,
`V = A + Bv + Cv²`, `W = C/4 + Tv`, with `(A,B,C,T)` the order-`q_s = 1587/1000` coefficients of
`lem:fqe-near-uniform-moment`, `(b, c)` those of the HT multiplier row, `d = 1/125`, `r = q_s - 1`,
`L⁺ = 6931471808/10^10 > ln 2`.  On five boxes every tensor Bernstein coefficient of `G` is positive
(generated by `gen_nu_cells.py`); the identity `G = Σ b_{ij} B_i(s) B_j(w)` on each box is checked by `ring`.
-/

